                <pb facs="0440" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.105A/9–2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Iran</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-22T20:00:00-04:00">September 22,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>581. British Embassy states Schwarzkopf has asked War for additional personnel to
                    enable him to assume responsibility for Iranian police and that War has refused
                    the request. However, responsible War official informs Dept that no such request
                    has been received from Schwarzkopf. Please report on status of this matter.</p>
                <p>For your information British have again expressed to Dept their preoccupation
                    over security situation in postwar Iran and urged Dept to do everything possible
                    to strengthen Iranian Army, <hi rendition="#italic">Gendarmerie</hi> and Police.
                    While regretting withdrawal of the Ridley Mission they welcome renewal of
                    Schwarzkopf contract for additional year. They urge strengthening of latter
                    mission to enable it to assume responsibility for Iranian police or
                    alternatively assignment of a separate police mission.</p>
                <p>Dept is entirely favorable to the idea of keeping the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gendarmerie</hi> Mission in Iran and of strengthening it as much as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
